terms.medium_def:
A location only mentioned at Act.17.1; 
only referred to as Amphipolis (Ἀμφίπολις). § Amphipolis, "a city surrounded" or "a city conspicuous" 
Amphipolis, a city of Thrace, on the river Strymon, Acts 17:1*

A location only mentioned at Col.4.13; 
only referred to as Hierapolis (Ἱεράπολις). § Hierapolis, "[pagan] sacred city" 
Hierapolis, a city of Phrygia, Col. 4:13*

A location only mentioned at Act.16.11; 
only referred to as Neapolis (Νεάπολις). § Neapolis, "new city" 
Neapolis, a city of Thrace on the Strymonic gulf, Acts 16:11*

A location first mentioned at Tit.3.12; 
only referred to as Nicopolis (Νικόπολις). § Nicopolis, "victory city" 
Nicopolis, a city of Macedonia, Tit. 3:12*

A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.11.24; 
referred to as Terah (תֶּ֫רַח), or Terah (KJV= Thara) (Θάρα); 
a son of Nahor; 
father of Abraham, Nahor, Haran and Sarah.

A man of the Greeks living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.10.4; 
only referred to as Tarshish (תַּרְשִׁישׁ); 
son of Javan; 
a brother of Elishah, Kittim and Dodanim. §son of Javan

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.7.10; 
only referred to as Tarshish (תַּרְשִׁישׁ); 
son of Bilhan; 
a brother of Jeush, Benjamin, Ehud, Chenaanah, Zethan and Ahishahar.

A man from the tribe of Asher living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.7.37; 
only referred to as Hod (הוֹד); 
son of Zophah; 
a brother of Suah, Harnepher, Shual, Beri, Imrah, Bezer, Shamma, Shilshah, Ithran and Beera. § one of the sons of Zophah, among the descendants of Asher

A man from the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.3.24; 
referred to as Hodaviah (הוֹדַוְיָה), or Hodaiah (=Ketiv) (הוֹדַיְוָהוּ); 
son of Elioenai; 
a brother of Eliashib, Pelaiah, Akkub, Johanan, Delaiah and Anani.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at 1Ch.9.7; 
only referred to as Hodaviah (הוֹדַוְיָה); 
a son of Hassenuah; 
father of Meshullam.

A woman(?) from the tribe of Judah(?) living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.4.19; 
only referred to as Hodiah (הוֹדִיָּה); 
sister of Naham; 
wife of Ishbah(?). § one of the two wives of Ezra, a man of Judah

David's brother from the tribe of Judah living at the time of United Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.2.14; 
only referred to as Raddai (רַדַּי); 
son of Jesse; 
a brother of David, Eliab, Abinadab, Shimeah, Nethanel, Ozem, Zeruiah, Abigail(?) and Elihu. § the 5th son of Jesse and brother of David
